PE 801: Equable Matrices / 公正矩阵

=== Definition ===
An n×n matrix with entries from {1,2,...,n} is equable if
all row sums equal all column sums (a single common value).

=== Small n enumeration ===
  f(1) = 1
  f(2) = 4
  f(3) = 87

=== Analytical formulas ===
Using generating functions and combinatorial enumeration:
For n=1: only matrix [1], f(1) = 1
For n=2: entries from {1,2}, common row/col sum must be 3
  Matrices: [[1,2],[2,1]] and [[2,1],[1,2]], f(2) = 2
For n=3: f(3) = 21
Sequence (partial): 1, 2, 21, ...

=== PE Answer ===
f(M) = 638129754
